:: Night Shift 2 [event main_quest] {"position":"6200,500","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "The Night Shift" (main_nightShift), last part, STAGE1_PROPOSAL.md 4.12. $club.name. If they went
   ($flags.supplierOffered): the door, the doorman, members only, and me in the car outside. If I paid: the deal in the back
   office, alone. Either way, at 11:40 p.m. $ethan.name calls. The choice sets $flags.answeredEthan:
     true   "Where are you? I need to talk to you. Come to the office." "Tomorrow."
     false  a voicemail I don't listen to until morning
   The way home is Night Shift 3. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[7].img>><</silent>>
$club.name doesn't have a sign. It has a black door between a closed bank and a shoe repair shop, a doorman in a dark coat, and a small brass plate with a number on it that you'd only notice if you were looking for it.

/* MEDIA: images/events/night_shift/door.jpg | A black door on a dark downtown street, a doorman in a long coat, a single brass number plate, rain on the pavement */

<<if $flags.supplierOffered === true>>
I park across the street. Neither of them has said a word the whole way. In the rearview mirror I can see their hands, still linked on the seat between them.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Ask for $supplier.callName at the door. He's expecting you. I'll be right here." },
{ text: "$mom.callName nods. $sister.callName nods. Then $mom.callName squeezes her hand once, lets go, and opens her door." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

They cross the street together, in the rain, in the black dresses and the heels, $mom.callName half a step ahead the way she walks when she's taking someone to the doctor. The doorman looks at them, then at a list on his phone, then steps aside and opens the black door.

$sister.callName looks back once, at the car. I don't know if she can see me through the windshield. I don't touch my ear.

The door closes behind them.

<<else>>
The doorman takes my name and my phone and walks me through a dark room full of low music and lower voices, past a long bar and a row of velvet booths, to a door at the back marked PRIVATE. $supplier.callName is behind a desk with a glass of something amber and a small aluminum case.

<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $supplier, text: "$player.name. Punctual. And alone. You'd be amazed how rare both of those are." },
{ text: "He slides the case across the desk without opening it." },
{ who: $supplier, text: "Everything on your list. The instructions are inside. Read them twice. My customers who read them once don't stay my customers for long." },
{ who: $player, text: "Thank you." },
{ who: $supplier, text: "Don't thank me. Just come back. Everyone comes back." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

The whole thing takes six minutes. On my way out, a woman in one of the velvet booths is laughing at something a man is saying with his hand on her knee, and she looks up at me as I pass, and then away.

I sit in the car outside for a while with the case on the passenger seat, not starting the engine.
<</if>>

<<linkreplace "Wait">>
<<silently>><<AdvanceTimeTo 6>><</silently>>
The rain gets heavier. The doorman stands under the awning and smokes. Nobody comes out. The clock on the dashboard says 11:39, and then it says 11:40.

My phone lights up on the seat beside me.

<i>$ethan.name</i>

/* MEDIA: images/events/night_shift/phone.jpg | A phone lighting up on a car seat in the dark, rain on the windshield behind it */

He never calls. He texts, he sends memes at two in the morning, he leaves voice notes about pizza. He doesn't call.

It keeps ringing.

<div id="ns-choice">
<div><<link `"Answer " + $ethan.name`>><<replace "#ns-choice">>
<<silently>>
<<set _msgs = [
{ who: $player, text: "Hey. What's up?" },
{ who: $ethan, text: "Where are you?" },
{ text: "There's no joke first, and he doesn't call me boss. His voice sounds wrong, flat and very awake, somewhere with an echo." },
{ who: $player, text: "A meeting. I told you. What's going on?" },
{ who: $ethan, text: "I need to talk to you. Tonight. Can you come to the office?" },
{ text: "Across the street, the black door stays closed. Somewhere behind it are the two people I live with." },
{ who: $player, text: "Tomorrow. First thing. I can't tonight." },
{ text: "There's a long silence on the line. Long enough that I check whether the call dropped." },
{ who: $ethan, text: "Tomorrow. Okay." },
{ text: "He hangs up without saying goodbye. He always says goodbye. He usually says it twice." },
]>>
<</silently>>
<<Chat _msgs>>

I look at the phone for a while. Then I put it face down on the seat and look at the black door again.

<<set $flags.answeredEthan to true>>
<div class="navigation-link"><<link "Later" "Night Shift 3">><</link>></div>
<</replace>><</link>></div>
<div><<link "Let it ring">><<replace "#ns-choice">>
I let it ring. It rings for a long time. Then it stops, and a minute later the screen lights up again: <i>1 new voicemail</i>.

I don't listen to it. Whatever it is, it's $ethan.name, and $ethan.name can wait until tomorrow. I put the phone face down on the seat and look at the black door again.

<<set $flags.answeredEthan to false>>
<div class="navigation-link"><<link "Later" "Night Shift 3">><</link>></div>
<</replace>><</link>></div>
</div>

<</linkreplace>>


:: Night Shift 3 [event main_quest] {"position":"6325,500","size":"100,100"}
/* Quest "The Night Shift" (main_nightShift), the end: after the call. If they went, the car home, the two of them in the
   back seat, in silence, and $sister.callName sleeps in $mom.callName's room. If I paid, home alone with the case. Ends the
   quest; The Morning After is next. */
<<silent>><<SetBackground $locations[7].img>><</silent>>
<<if $flags.supplierOffered === true>>
They come out at ten past two.

The doorman holds the door. $mom.callName comes first, with her coat on and buttoned to the neck, and $sister.callName right behind her, holding her heels in one hand. Neither of them looks at the car until they're halfway across the street.

They get into the back seat. Both of them. Nobody says anything.

I drive home through empty streets, under the orange lights, with the rain on the windshield and the wipers going. In the rearview mirror, every time we pass under a streetlight, I can see them: $sister.callName with her head on $mom.callName's shoulder, eyes open, looking at nothing. $mom.callName with her arm around her, looking out the window. Their hands linked again on the seat.

Nobody says a single word the whole way home.

At the house they go upstairs together, and I hear $mom.callName's door close, and then, after a minute, $sister.callName's door doesn't close at all, because she's in $mom.callName's room.

I sit at the kitchen table in the dark for a long time. My phone is still face down. I don't turn it over.

<<UpdateStat "+" "MomCorruption" 5>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterCorruption" 5>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "MomResistance" 5>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "SisterResistance" 5>>
<<UpdateStat "+" "Corruption" 5>>
<<Feel $mom "player" -2>>
<<Feel $sister "player" -2>>
<<Feel $mom "supplier" -3 "lasting">>
<<Feel $sister "supplier" -3 "lasting">>
<<ProfileLog $mom "The Last Night" "I drove her and $sister.callName to $supplier.callName's club in the black dresses I picked, and waited outside. In the back seat they saw each other and understood. They came out at ten past two and didn't say a word the whole way home. She took $sister.callName into her room.">>
<<ProfileLog $sister "The Last Night" "I drove her and $mom.callName to $supplier.callName's club, the way we rehearsed it, and waited outside. In the back seat she saw $mom.callName, and they both knew. They came out at ten past two. She slept in $mom.callName's room.">>
<<else>>
I drive home with the case on the passenger seat. The streets are empty. At home everyone's asleep, $mom.callName's door closed, $sister.callName's light off.

I put the case in my desk drawer, next to the Anchor and the Catalyst and the original, and sit on my bed for a long time with my phone face down on the nightstand.
<</if>>

<<NextQuest $player>>
<<ReturnFromEvent "Go to bed" "Bedroom">>
